00:09:50.320 --> 00:09:55.040
roughly 15 to 20% of rhinoplasty

00:09:52.520 --> 00:09:57.000
patients eventually undergo a second

00:09:55.040 --> 00:09:59.360
revision surgery to fix the first

00:09:57.000 --> 00:10:01.320
surgery. And those were only reported

00:09:59.360 --> 00:10:02.960
statistics, which means the real numbers

00:10:01.320 --> 00:10:05.040
are likely much higher. So, I didn't

00:10:02.960 --> 00:10:06.960
know that when I went into this. And in

00:10:05.040 --> 00:10:08.760
hindsight, the amount of change that was

00:10:06.960 --> 00:10:10.760
done to my nose may have been too

00:10:08.760 --> 00:10:12.680
aggressive. I felt like I had changed my

00:10:10.760 --> 00:10:14.600
face for the better, but very quickly,

00:10:12.680 --> 00:10:16.120
things started to go in a completely

00:10:14.600 --> 00:10:18.760
different direction. Things started to

00:10:16.120 --> 00:10:20.120
go wrong for me about 6 weeks post-op.

00:10:18.760 --> 00:10:21.400
Up until that point, I thought I was

00:10:20.120 --> 00:10:22.920
healing normally, even though the

00:10:21.400 --> 00:10:24.640
redness was still there. And I thought

00:10:22.920 --> 00:10:26.360
eventually, that was also going to go

00:10:24.640 --> 00:10:28.840
away, maybe by the second or third

00:10:26.360 --> 00:10:31.080
month. So, I took all my medications. I

00:10:28.840 --> 00:10:33.760
did everything I was told. I sent photos

00:10:31.080 --> 00:10:36.640
to the surgical team every week. And I

00:10:33.760 --> 00:10:38.480
focused so much on my recovery, on my

00:10:36.640 --> 00:10:39.760
healing. And I was trying to learn

00:10:38.480 --> 00:10:42.160
everything that I could about the

00:10:39.760 --> 00:10:44.200
redness in my skin. But then, I started

00:10:42.160 --> 00:10:47.160
noticing something strange. My nose

00:10:44.200 --> 00:10:49.640
started to swell up a lot. And it was

00:10:47.160 --> 00:10:51.120
not the regular normal rhinoplasty

00:10:49.640 --> 00:10:53.080
swelling that you get, because usually

00:10:51.120 --> 00:10:55.080
after surgery, your nose will swell up

00:10:53.080 --> 00:10:57.480
and down, up and down for about a year.

00:10:55.080 --> 00:11:01.120
But this was very different. It was

00:10:57.480 --> 00:11:03.880
getting a lot bigger and redder day by

00:11:01.120 --> 00:11:06.120
day. I was taking photos every day,

00:11:03.880 --> 00:11:09.520
sending photos to the medical team

00:11:06.120 --> 00:11:11.480
almost daily, asking what was going on.

00:11:09.520 --> 00:11:13.240
And the medical assistant kept saying

00:11:11.480 --> 00:11:15.120
the same thing. It was part of the

00:11:13.240 --> 00:11:16.720
healing process. Swelling can happen.

00:11:15.120 --> 00:11:18.960
It's normal. Everything should settle

00:11:16.720 --> 00:11:21.040
down. I even scheduled a video call with

00:11:18.960 --> 00:11:22.400
the surgeon, and he also assured me that

00:11:21.040 --> 00:11:24.360
everything looked fine. And I just

00:11:22.400 --> 00:11:26.520
needed time to heal. And it was probably

00:11:24.360 --> 00:11:29.000
a healing response. But the swelling

00:11:26.520 --> 00:11:31.800
kept getting worse. The tip of my nose

00:11:29.000 --> 00:11:34.560
turned bright red. Eventually, it looked

00:11:31.800 --> 00:11:36.080
like a giant red ball. At one point, it

00:11:34.560 --> 00:11:37.840
literally resembled Rudolph the

00:11:36.080 --> 00:11:40.360
Red-Nosed Reindeer. And at that point, I

00:11:37.840 --> 00:11:42.040
decided to go see a local dermatologist

00:11:40.360 --> 00:11:43.360
because the redness was showing up on my

00:11:42.040 --> 00:11:45.160
skin. I thought maybe it was some kind

00:11:43.360 --> 00:11:46.920
of skin complication. But then, the

00:11:45.160 --> 00:11:48.680
dermatologist told me they weren't

00:11:46.920 --> 00:11:50.040
exactly sure what was happening either.

00:11:48.680 --> 00:11:51.760
They were suspecting maybe it's an

00:11:50.040 --> 00:11:53.920
infection and prescribed a

00:11:51.760 --> 00:11:55.880
broad-spectrum antibiotic while they

00:11:53.920 --> 00:11:57.840
sent my sample out for bacterial

00:11:55.880 --> 00:11:59.320
testing. I remember telling them that I

00:11:57.840 --> 00:12:01.640
went to Turkey to get a nose job. And

00:11:59.320 --> 00:12:04.400
the look on that provider's face was

00:12:01.640 --> 00:12:06.160
extremely judgmental and was just like,

00:12:04.400 --> 00:12:08.280
"You should have never gone there. You

00:12:06.160 --> 00:12:10.680
messed up. You should have stayed there

00:12:08.280 --> 00:12:12.720
for at least a few months to recover or

00:12:10.680 --> 00:12:14.600
get it done here in the US." But they're

00:12:12.720 --> 00:12:16.960
also like, "We have no idea what's going

00:12:14.600 --> 00:12:18.320
on with you." So, I went home and I did

00:12:16.960 --> 00:12:20.240
everything I was supposed to. I took the

00:12:18.320 --> 00:12:22.440
antibiotics exactly as prescribed, every

00:12:20.240 --> 00:12:24.440
single dose of it. But day by day, that

00:12:22.440 --> 00:12:27.080
swelling kept getting worse. And after

00:12:24.440 --> 00:12:29.000
10 days, it looked insane and genuinely

00:12:27.080 --> 00:12:30.080
concerning. I went back before my

00:12:29.000 --> 00:12:32.480
scheduled appointment, which was

00:12:30.080 --> 00:12:34.280
supposed to be 2 weeks for my follow-up,

00:12:32.480 --> 00:12:35.760
and I asked them, "Have you received the

00:12:34.280 --> 00:12:38.160
bacterial results yet?" And they told me

00:12:35.760 --> 00:12:39.880
something that was so shocking to me.

00:12:38.160 --> 00:12:41.960
They said that they had received the

00:12:39.880 --> 00:12:43.920
results the day after my first

00:12:41.960 --> 00:12:45.880
appointment, but obviously they never

00:12:43.920 --> 00:12:47.960
called me to tell me that or to switch

00:12:45.880 --> 00:12:49.640
out my antibiotics because my

00:12:47.960 --> 00:12:51.800
antibiotics that I was taking at the

00:12:49.640 --> 00:12:53.880
time did not work for the bacteria that

00:12:51.800 --> 00:12:56.000
I had. So, it turns out the bacteria I

00:12:53.880 --> 00:12:58.560
had was extremely resistant to

00:12:56.000 --> 00:13:00.000
medication. So, then I asked them, "Why

00:12:58.560 --> 00:13:01.280
didn't you ever contact with me when the

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:04.120
results came in?" And they said it was

00:13:01.280 --> 00:13:05.720
just not in their protocol to call their

00:13:04.120 --> 00:13:07.400
patients about lab results when they

00:13:05.720 --> 00:13:09.040
received them. Also, "You should have

00:13:07.400 --> 00:13:10.560
never gone to Turkey. This was kind of

00:13:09.040 --> 00:13:12.520
your fault and the surgeon's fault that

00:13:10.560 --> 00:13:15.440
this happened. Don't blame us. Blame

00:13:12.520 --> 00:13:17.600
him." And I was just like, "Whoa, that's

00:13:15.440 --> 00:13:18.960
messed up." They sent me off without

00:13:17.600 --> 00:13:20.080
anything, without any medication or

00:13:18.960 --> 00:13:21.800
anything. They were just like, "Uh let

00:13:20.080 --> 00:13:23.680
me just call my boss, who's a plastic

00:13:21.800 --> 00:13:25.680
surgeon." And then later that night, I

00:13:23.680 --> 00:13:28.480
got a call from their office telling me

00:13:25.680 --> 00:13:30.320
to go to the ER immediately. At that

00:13:28.480 --> 00:13:32.160
point they realized that the infection

00:13:30.320 --> 00:13:33.800
was coming from my rhinoplasty and that

00:13:32.160 --> 00:13:36.240
I needed a much, much stronger

00:13:33.800 --> 00:13:38.920
antibiotic right away. And by then, it

00:13:36.240 --> 00:13:40.800
had already become a medical emergency.

00:13:38.920 --> 00:13:42.840
So that night I went to the ER and I

00:13:40.800 --> 00:13:45.600
ended up hospitalized for a little more

00:13:42.840 --> 00:13:48.120
than 1 week. That night in the ER was

00:13:45.600 --> 00:13:50.840
one of the most surreal and traumatic

00:13:48.120 --> 00:13:52.440
nights I have ever experienced within an

00:13:50.840 --> 00:13:54.840
emergency medical environment because

00:13:52.440 --> 00:13:56.920
the ER was completely chaotic. There

00:13:54.840 --> 00:13:58.840
were people coming in who were in car

00:13:56.920 --> 00:14:00.520
accidents, yelling and screaming in

00:13:58.840 --> 00:14:02.640
pain. There were also people

00:14:00.520 --> 00:14:04.840
experiencing severe mental health

00:14:02.640 --> 00:14:06.600
crises. There were police officers there

00:14:04.840 --> 00:14:08.640
dealing with situations involving

00:14:06.600 --> 00:14:10.480
patients who were so-called regulars in

00:14:08.640 --> 00:14:12.240
the ER. It was just an incredibly

00:14:10.480 --> 00:14:13.760
high-stress environment and I had no

00:14:12.240 --> 00:14:15.560
idea how the people who work there could

00:14:13.760 --> 00:14:17.760
handle that kind of environment. I was

00:14:15.560 --> 00:14:19.120
just sitting there watching everything

00:14:17.760 --> 00:14:21.320
unfold in front of me and it made me

00:14:19.120 --> 00:14:23.080
realize how intense emergency medicine

00:14:21.320 --> 00:14:24.120
really is. These doctors and nurses

00:14:23.080 --> 00:14:26.120
there are dealing with extreme

00:14:24.120 --> 00:14:27.640
situations every single hour. And I got

00:14:26.120 --> 00:14:29.760
to the ER around 7:00 or 8:00 p.m. that

00:14:27.640 --> 00:14:32.680
night and I didn't get a hospital bed or

00:14:29.760 --> 00:14:34.160
admitted into the hospital until 2:00 in

00:14:32.680 --> 00:14:36.040
the morning. But when they finally

00:14:34.160 --> 00:14:38.240
admitted me, immediately they started me

00:14:36.040 --> 00:14:40.400
on IV antibiotics. And then by the next

00:14:38.240 --> 00:14:42.160
day, I was evaluated by an ENT

00:14:40.400 --> 00:14:44.680
specialist, ear, nose, and throat

00:14:42.160 --> 00:14:46.480
surgeon. So he came back to me with the

00:14:44.680 --> 00:14:48.440
conclusion that the infection was so

00:14:46.480 --> 00:14:50.720
severe that it needed to be surgically

00:14:48.440 --> 00:14:53.200
removed. 6 weeks after my original

00:14:50.720 --> 00:14:56.080
rhinoplasty, I had to undergo this

00:14:53.200 --> 00:14:58.200
emergency surgery to try and remove the

00:14:56.080 --> 00:15:00.560
infection from my nose. So that's a

00:14:58.200 --> 00:15:02.440
second surgery in 6 weeks and that's

00:15:00.560 --> 00:15:03.640
when things got even more complicated.

00:15:02.440 --> 00:15:05.480
So while I was at the hospital, the

00:15:03.640 --> 00:15:07.680
doctors ran more scans and tests to

00:15:05.480 --> 00:15:09.320
figure out exactly what was going on and

00:15:07.680 --> 00:15:11.880
that's when I learned what was actually,

00:15:09.320 --> 00:15:13.920
I guess, on my nose. It wasn't just

00:15:11.880 --> 00:15:16.480
swelling, but it was an abscess, a

00:15:13.920 --> 00:15:18.440
pocket of pus created by the bacterial

00:15:16.480 --> 00:15:21.440
infection. And the abscess that was on

00:15:18.440 --> 00:15:23.440
the tip of my nose was about 2 cm in

00:15:21.440 --> 00:15:25.520
diameter and that's about an inch, which

00:15:23.440 --> 00:15:27.920
is very large considering that's the

00:15:25.520 --> 00:15:30.000
whole size of my nose. So, the emergency

00:15:27.920 --> 00:15:32.160
surgery I had was to make an incision, a

00:15:30.000 --> 00:15:34.960
cut on the tip of my nose, and drain the

00:15:32.160 --> 00:15:37.680
abscess. But the situation was worse

00:15:34.960 --> 00:15:39.760
than just the abscess itself. The CT

00:15:37.680 --> 00:15:42.880
scan showed that the bacteria had

00:15:39.760 --> 00:15:45.680
already caused severe damage to the

00:15:42.880 --> 00:15:47.840
internal structure of my nose and at

00:15:45.680 --> 00:15:50.040
that point the infection had eaten

00:15:47.840 --> 00:15:52.800
through a large portion of the rib

00:15:50.040 --> 00:15:55.680
cartilage graft that was used to build

00:15:52.800 --> 00:15:58.320
up my nose. So, half of the structural

00:15:55.680 --> 00:16:00.400
support of my nose was essentially gone.

00:15:58.320 --> 00:16:02.440
My nose was already in a state of

00:16:00.400 --> 00:16:03.800
partial collapse. At that point the

00:16:02.440 --> 00:16:05.520
doctors were also concerned about

00:16:03.800 --> 00:16:07.800
something that's even more serious than

00:16:05.520 --> 00:16:10.960
that and life-threatening, which was

00:16:07.800 --> 00:16:13.120
sepsis. Sepsis happens when an infection

00:16:10.960 --> 00:16:15.280
spreads into the bloodstream and

00:16:13.120 --> 00:16:18.200
triggers a full-body inflammatory

00:16:15.280 --> 00:16:19.920
response. This in itself is already a

00:16:18.200 --> 00:16:22.080
life-threatening medical emergency and

00:16:19.920 --> 00:16:24.680
because this infection was located in

00:16:22.080 --> 00:16:26.880
the center of my face and had already

00:16:24.680 --> 00:16:29.480
progressed so significantly that I had

00:16:26.880 --> 00:16:30.720
gone to the ER so late at that point,

00:16:29.480 --> 00:16:33.120
the doctors were worried that it could

00:16:30.720 --> 00:16:35.320
escalate [music] into septic shock. And

00:16:33.120 --> 00:16:38.000
if septic shock is not treated within 12

00:16:35.320 --> 00:16:40.120
hours, it has a very high mortality

00:16:38.000 --> 00:16:42.400
rate, which means I could very well end

00:16:40.120 --> 00:16:45.320
up alive at that point if I had waited a

00:16:42.400 --> 00:16:47.839
day later. So, I was extremely ill. I

00:16:45.320 --> 00:16:49.400
had high fever. My blood pressure had

00:16:47.839 --> 00:16:51.960
dropped dangerously low. I was

00:16:49.400 --> 00:16:53.720
delirious, completely out of it for the

00:16:51.960 --> 00:16:55.880
whole hospital stay, and my mental

00:16:53.720 --> 00:16:58.240
health was so low that I did nothing

00:16:55.880 --> 00:17:00.120
else [music] except sleep and cry. And

00:16:58.240 --> 00:17:02.320
they were constantly pumping me with

00:17:00.120 --> 00:17:04.480
fluids and antibiotics. Looking back at

00:17:02.320 --> 00:17:06.720
this, I realize how dangerous the

00:17:04.480 --> 00:17:08.720
situation was because sepsis can

00:17:06.720 --> 00:17:10.560
progress extremely quickly. If I had

00:17:08.720 --> 00:17:12.760
gone to the hospital any later than I

00:17:10.560 --> 00:17:15.040
did, I could have deteriorated so

00:17:12.760 --> 00:17:17.800
quickly. So, when I say that I am lucky

00:17:15.040 --> 00:17:19.160
to be here today, I really mean that.

00:17:17.800 --> 00:17:21.000
And while I was at the hospital, I

00:17:19.160 --> 00:17:23.160
called my surgeon so he could see what

00:17:21.000 --> 00:17:24.800
happened. And he was extremely

00:17:23.160 --> 00:17:26.800
apologetic. He wanted to fix the

00:17:24.800 --> 00:17:28.520
situation. He told me he wanted to take

00:17:26.800 --> 00:17:30.160
accountability. He told me he was

00:17:28.520 --> 00:17:31.640
completely responsible for what

00:17:30.160 --> 00:17:33.280
happened, especially because it was

00:17:31.640 --> 00:17:37.000
known to us at that point that the

00:17:33.280 --> 00:17:38.960
bacteria is hospital acquired, meaning I

00:17:37.000 --> 00:17:41.000
got infected during the surgery. And

00:17:38.960 --> 00:17:43.000
these hospital acquired bacteria are

00:17:41.000 --> 00:17:45.840
like super [music] bacteria. They're

00:17:43.000 --> 00:17:47.440
extremely resistant, extremely strong.

00:17:45.840 --> 00:17:49.320
And so I didn't get this because I

00:17:47.440 --> 00:17:51.000
wasn't washing my nose correctly or

00:17:49.320 --> 00:17:52.240
whatever. And he knew. He knew what

00:17:51.000 --> 00:17:53.840
happened. He said he wanted to fix the

00:17:52.240 --> 00:17:55.920
situation for me, but because we

00:17:53.840 --> 00:17:58.000
couldn't do anything immediately after a

00:17:55.920 --> 00:17:59.920
traumatic infection like this, we have

00:17:58.000 --> 00:18:02.040
to let the tissue stabilize before even

00:17:59.920 --> 00:18:03.360
attempting any kind of revision surgery.

00:18:02.040 --> 00:18:05.160
At that point, I was about to have two

00:18:03.360 --> 00:18:07.320
surgeries in 6 weeks. In most cases,

00:18:05.160 --> 00:18:10.600
surgeons recommend 10 to 12 months at

00:18:07.320 --> 00:18:12.440
least before performing another revision

00:18:10.600 --> 00:18:14.480
rhinoplasty. And then the day after that

00:18:12.440 --> 00:18:16.400
call, I remembered I had the emergency

00:18:14.480 --> 00:18:18.240
surgery. So a week later, I was

00:18:16.400 --> 00:18:20.200
discharged. After a week, we're getting

00:18:18.240 --> 00:18:22.040
out of here finally, huh? You'll be all

00:18:20.200 --> 00:18:24.000
right. You got it. You got it. But the

00:18:22.040 --> 00:18:27.760
treatment didn't stop there. I was sent

00:18:24.000 --> 00:18:29.880
home with 1 month full of IV antibiotics

00:18:27.760 --> 00:18:32.160
that I had to administer myself. I had

00:18:29.880 --> 00:18:34.560
to do this three times a day, every 8

00:18:32.160 --> 00:18:36.480
hours on the hour. I was waking up every

00:18:34.560 --> 00:18:38.200
morning at 5:00 a.m. My husband was also

00:18:36.480 --> 00:18:40.680
helping me with this every morning. I

00:18:38.200 --> 00:18:42.680
had to have a catheter attached into my

00:18:40.680 --> 00:18:44.520
veins so that the antibiotics can enter

00:18:42.680 --> 00:18:46.560
my bloodstream directly. So the

00:18:44.520 --> 00:18:49.600
antibiotic that they put me on is called

00:18:46.560 --> 00:18:52.080
meropenem, which is one of the strongest

00:18:49.600 --> 00:18:54.200
antibiotics used and is usually reserved

00:18:52.080 --> 00:18:56.080
for a very, very severe hospital

00:18:54.200 --> 00:18:58.280
acquired infection. And it had a lot of

00:18:56.080 --> 00:19:00.080
its own severe side effects as well

00:18:58.280 --> 00:19:02.440
because some of these side effects were

00:19:00.080 --> 00:19:05.400
also potentially fatal reactions amongst

00:19:02.440 --> 00:19:08.000
other things. So it severely disrupted

00:19:05.400 --> 00:19:10.160
my entire health, especially my gut

00:19:08.000 --> 00:19:12.960
microbiome. It just wiped everything

00:19:10.160 --> 00:19:15.840
out. In the medical world, meropenem is

00:19:12.960 --> 00:19:17.640
a last resort antibiotic for extremely

00:19:15.840 --> 00:19:18.640
severe bacterial infections, but in my

00:19:17.640 --> 00:19:20.080
case,

00:19:18.640 --> 00:19:21.720
it was also life saving because there

00:19:20.080 --> 00:19:23.120
weren't many other options. But, a large

00:19:21.720 --> 00:19:25.040
portion of my gut microbiome was

00:19:23.120 --> 00:19:27.200
basically gone, which I continued to

00:19:25.040 --> 00:19:30.120
suffer the effects of that for almost an

00:19:27.200 --> 00:19:31.600
entire year after what happened. And

00:19:30.120 --> 00:19:33.480
during this whole time, I stayed in

00:19:31.600 --> 00:19:36.400
close contact with my rhinoplasty

00:19:33.480 --> 00:19:38.280
surgeon. I actually asked him to cover

00:19:36.400 --> 00:19:40.760
the cost of the skin treatments that I

00:19:38.280 --> 00:19:42.200
needed to recover from the damage. And,

00:19:40.760 --> 00:19:44.520
you know what? To his credit, he agreed

00:19:42.200 --> 00:19:47.080
to do that for me. He paid for that. So,

00:19:44.520 --> 00:19:49.120
I found a dermatologist who specialized

00:19:47.080 --> 00:19:50.680
in laser treatment for nasal scars. That

00:19:49.120 --> 00:19:53.560
dermatologist had a lot of photos of

00:19:50.680 --> 00:19:55.720
fixing all kinds of traumatic scars,

00:19:53.560 --> 00:19:57.560
rhinophyma. He's one of the top

00:19:55.720 --> 00:19:59.320
dermatologists in the United States. So,

00:19:57.560 --> 00:20:00.560
it's definitely not the initial

00:19:59.320 --> 00:20:02.320
dermatologist I went to because they

00:20:00.560 --> 00:20:04.800
were completely useless and

00:20:02.320 --> 00:20:07.200
victim-blaming and neglectful. And I

00:20:04.800 --> 00:20:10.320
underwent three ablative laser sessions,

00:20:07.200 --> 00:20:12.440
and every session left me bloody. I had

00:20:10.320 --> 00:20:14.360
to recover for at least 10 days, and I

00:20:12.440 --> 00:20:15.920
went back about once a month. Those

00:20:14.360 --> 00:20:18.160
treatments actually helped me to

00:20:15.920 --> 00:20:19.720
stabilize my nasal skin and reduce the

00:20:18.160 --> 00:20:22.400
scarring on the tip of my nose because

00:20:19.720 --> 00:20:25.200
it looked so scary. Like, there were

00:20:22.400 --> 00:20:27.680
three giant bumps on my nose that were

00:20:25.200 --> 00:20:29.800
very hard raised scars. I still have

00:20:27.680 --> 00:20:32.840
some scarring there today, which I will

00:20:29.800 --> 00:20:34.600
continue treating with laser probably in

00:20:32.840 --> 00:20:36.720
the near future. But, after that third

00:20:34.600 --> 00:20:39.320
session, the tip of my nose had become

00:20:36.720 --> 00:20:40.720
extremely thin, the the skin that is.

00:20:39.320 --> 00:20:42.120
And I I didn't feel comfortable

00:20:40.720 --> 00:20:43.400
continuing with more treatments, so I

00:20:42.120 --> 00:20:45.160
stopped. And that's when I started

00:20:43.400 --> 00:20:47.720
preparing for the final step, which was

00:20:45.160 --> 00:20:49.520
to go back to Turkey for a revision

00:20:47.720 --> 00:20:51.680
planoplasty, where the surgeon was going

00:20:49.520 --> 00:20:53.880
to try and rebuild the nose that the

00:20:51.680 --> 00:20:55.840
infection had destroyed. So, at this

00:20:53.880 --> 00:20:57.000
point in the story, some of you probably

00:20:55.840 --> 00:20:58.920
have a lot of questions, but before we

00:20:57.000 --> 00:21:00.520
move on to what happened next,

00:20:58.920 --> 00:21:02.280
I want to talk about something that was

00:21:00.520 --> 00:21:04.080
just as difficult as the medical side of

00:21:02.280 --> 00:21:05.720
this, which was my mental health during

00:21:04.080 --> 00:21:07.800
this whole year. This was one of the

00:21:05.720 --> 00:21:09.520
most difficult health experiences I've

00:21:07.800 --> 00:21:11.800
ever gone through and it greatly

00:21:09.520 --> 00:21:13.440
affected my mental health and I know

00:21:11.800 --> 00:21:15.080
nobody else saw it happen except for the

00:21:13.440 --> 00:21:17.720
two people in my life, my husband and my

00:21:15.080 --> 00:21:20.240
mom, people closest to me, family. And

00:21:17.720 --> 00:21:21.880
the only thing that comes close was

00:21:20.240 --> 00:21:24.120
another recent time in my life when the

00:21:21.880 --> 00:21:25.600
doctors and I thought that for months I

00:21:24.120 --> 00:21:28.080
had cancer.

00:21:25.600 --> 00:21:31.720
Eventually it turned out not to be the

00:21:28.080 --> 00:21:33.560
case, thankfully, and I still keep that

00:21:31.720 --> 00:21:36.160
letter with me that says that I had no

00:21:33.560 --> 00:21:38.920
cancer with me, no symptoms. Just to

00:21:36.160 --> 00:21:41.360
remind myself of what happened at the

00:21:38.920 --> 00:21:43.800
time that I overcame that too and thank

00:21:41.360 --> 00:21:45.240
God like I didn't have it. But those

00:21:43.800 --> 00:21:48.120
months of not knowing if I have it or

00:21:45.240 --> 00:21:49.960
not was so scary. But what happened with

00:21:48.120 --> 00:21:51.800
my nose is it's very different. It

00:21:49.960 --> 00:21:53.080
wasn't just about being scared of what

00:21:51.800 --> 00:21:55.040
could potentially happen. I was

00:21:53.080 --> 00:21:56.840
literally living inside this problem

00:21:55.040 --> 00:21:58.520
that I can physically see on my face

00:21:56.840 --> 00:22:01.280
every single day. I would look into the

00:21:58.520 --> 00:22:03.240
mirror and cry and cry. But you know,

00:22:01.280 --> 00:22:05.960
strangely enough, I was also grateful

00:22:03.240 --> 00:22:07.440
that of all people this happened to me

00:22:05.960 --> 00:22:09.440
cuz this kind of experience could

00:22:07.440 --> 00:22:11.440
completely destroy someone's mental

00:22:09.440 --> 00:22:13.800
health. I was able to survive this

00:22:11.440 --> 00:22:16.080
because I'm mentally already very strong

00:22:13.800 --> 00:22:18.840
and maybe a bit delusional too. And I

00:22:16.080 --> 00:22:20.720
was able to somehow get through this. I

00:22:18.840 --> 00:22:22.400
actually found support groups for

00:22:20.720 --> 00:22:24.440
patients like me who were going through

00:22:22.400 --> 00:22:26.520
this type of medical trauma,

00:22:24.440 --> 00:22:28.960
specifically for rhinoplasty, and there

00:22:26.520 --> 00:22:31.120
were people in those groups wanting to

00:22:28.960 --> 00:22:33.160
end their life themselves for way, way

00:22:31.120 --> 00:22:35.320
less than what I went through. But I

00:22:33.160 --> 00:22:37.000
refused to accept the reality that I was

00:22:35.320 --> 00:22:39.400
living in because I knew that the

00:22:37.000 --> 00:22:42.080
situation was not permanent. Eventually

00:22:39.400 --> 00:22:43.520
I can fix this damage. Eventually, you

00:22:42.080 --> 00:22:46.160
know, the scars on my nose is going to

00:22:43.520 --> 00:22:48.200
heal. So mentally I kept choosing every

00:22:46.160 --> 00:22:50.000
day when I woke up over and over again

00:22:48.200 --> 00:22:51.400
not to attach my identity to what my

00:22:50.000 --> 00:22:53.560
face looked like during that time. And

00:22:51.400 --> 00:22:55.680
it got me through somehow. It did. Even

00:22:53.560 --> 00:22:57.360
though physically that was the reality

00:22:55.680 --> 00:22:58.800
that I was living in. If you have been

00:22:57.360 --> 00:23:00.640
watching my channel for a while, some of

00:22:58.800 --> 00:23:02.880
you guys may be wondering when did this

00:23:00.640 --> 00:23:04.760
happen? During this time I continued to

00:23:02.880 --> 00:23:06.480
post videos on my YouTube channel like

00:23:04.760 --> 00:23:07.680
normal. Of course there were a few

00:23:06.480 --> 00:23:09.000
people who I kind of noticed that

00:23:07.680 --> 00:23:10.320
something looked off of my nose. Like

00:23:09.000 --> 00:23:11.800
even though I was up front about the

00:23:10.320 --> 00:23:14.000
nose job, I said it multiple times in

00:23:11.800 --> 00:23:15.520
multiple videos. I was discussing it. It

00:23:14.000 --> 00:23:17.240
wasn't something I wanted to encourage

00:23:15.520 --> 00:23:18.480
at all. But a lot of girls were saying

00:23:17.240 --> 00:23:20.080
that I looked good. I was getting a lot

00:23:18.480 --> 00:23:21.240
of comments saying that I looked botched

00:23:20.080 --> 00:23:22.560
or saying that I should have never

00:23:21.240 --> 00:23:24.520
messed with my nose. I should have loved

00:23:22.560 --> 00:23:26.880
myself more because I looked horrible. I

00:23:24.520 --> 00:23:28.520
was disgusting. So many cruel comments.

00:23:26.880 --> 00:23:31.040
And it showed me a side of the internet

00:23:28.520 --> 00:23:34.120
that is so incredibly limited in its

00:23:31.040 --> 00:23:36.400
understanding and unnecessarily harsh

00:23:34.120 --> 00:23:38.640
about people's appearances, especially

00:23:36.400 --> 00:23:40.400
women's appearance. And of course they

00:23:38.640 --> 00:23:42.360
didn't know what I was going through at

00:23:40.400 --> 00:23:44.920
the time, especially considering that I

00:23:42.360 --> 00:23:47.240
have always been open and honest about

00:23:44.920 --> 00:23:49.600
sharing my journey with my physical

00:23:47.240 --> 00:23:52.160
changes and with my self-improvement.

00:23:49.600 --> 00:23:54.160
Because maybe a lot of people don't see

00:23:52.160 --> 00:23:56.080
many examples like that. I guess it was

00:23:54.160 --> 00:23:57.600
very jarring for a lot of people to see

00:23:56.080 --> 00:23:59.080
that I'm actually active doing the

00:23:57.600 --> 00:24:00.560
things I'm preaching. But isn't that

00:23:59.080 --> 00:24:02.520
what we should all expect anyway?

00:24:00.560 --> 00:24:03.680
Especially from someone like me who's

00:24:02.520 --> 00:24:05.280
talking about these things. I mean, do

00:24:03.680 --> 00:24:06.600
these people want to learn from a liar

00:24:05.280 --> 00:24:09.040
or from someone who doesn't actually do

00:24:06.600 --> 00:24:10.720
what they say or worse hide what they've

00:24:09.040 --> 00:24:12.880
done? It's one thing to say that these

00:24:10.720 --> 00:24:14.880
are people's medical records, which I

00:24:12.880 --> 00:24:17.000
completely respect. It's another thing

00:24:14.880 --> 00:24:18.240
for them to be like, I have always

00:24:17.000 --> 00:24:20.040
looked like this. What are you talking

00:24:18.240 --> 00:24:21.840
about? It's something else. It's not

00:24:20.040 --> 00:24:23.200
because I had surgery when when they had

00:24:21.840 --> 00:24:24.880
surgery. So, you know, they should be

00:24:23.200 --> 00:24:27.320
honest. There are two villains in this

00:24:24.880 --> 00:24:29.160
world. I always say this. One that does

00:24:27.320 --> 00:24:30.840
evil things and then one who tells the

00:24:29.160 --> 00:24:32.640
truth. So again, I was okay with being

00:24:30.840 --> 00:24:34.080
misunderstood. At least I can stand by

00:24:32.640 --> 00:24:35.320
it. But that's also one of the reasons

00:24:34.080 --> 00:24:37.440
why it took me so long to make this

00:24:35.320 --> 00:24:39.440
video. Like I didn't want the world to

00:24:37.440 --> 00:24:40.400
know what I was going through while I

00:24:39.440 --> 00:24:42.200
was going through it because I was

00:24:40.400 --> 00:24:44.520
recovering from a very serious medical

00:24:42.200 --> 00:24:46.360
trauma. While I was quietly trying to

00:24:44.520 --> 00:24:48.040
you know, recover, I tried to keep my

00:24:46.360 --> 00:24:50.560
circle extremely small during this time.

00:24:48.040 --> 00:24:52.600
Like I didn't leave the house much and I

00:24:50.560 --> 00:24:54.680
avoided seeing people that I knew so

00:24:52.600 --> 00:24:56.840
that they wouldn't be like staring at my

00:24:54.680 --> 00:24:58.160
nose or my face. So only a handful of

00:24:56.840 --> 00:25:00.160
people knew what was actually happening.

00:24:58.160 --> 00:25:01.640
So, my husband, my mom, and obviously

00:25:00.160 --> 00:25:03.360
like the medical team that was involved

00:25:01.640 --> 00:25:05.080
and that was it. Like, it's one thing

00:25:03.360 --> 00:25:06.520
for me to appear in front of the camera

00:25:05.080 --> 00:25:08.040
with all my lights and my makeup and

00:25:06.520 --> 00:25:09.600
stuff. It's another thing to see me in

00:25:08.040 --> 00:25:11.080
person. So, I made a very intentional

00:25:09.600 --> 00:25:12.920
decision that I will only talk about

00:25:11.080 --> 00:25:14.120
this experience after I healed because

00:25:12.920 --> 00:25:15.480
talking about trauma while you're still

00:25:14.120 --> 00:25:17.520
in it can be very destabilizing. I

00:25:15.480 --> 00:25:19.040
wanted to process things and recover and

00:25:17.520 --> 00:25:20.880
then come back and share from a more

00:25:19.040 --> 00:25:22.280
stable space. So, during this time, I

00:25:20.880 --> 00:25:23.600
focused on what I could control. I kept

00:25:22.280 --> 00:25:25.360
putting my message out to the world. I

00:25:23.600 --> 00:25:28.160
kept doing my thing, making my videos

00:25:25.360 --> 00:25:30.400
because I know life is bigger than any

00:25:28.160 --> 00:25:32.440
one problem that I was facing and I

00:25:30.400 --> 00:25:34.240
shouldn't stop my life because of this.

00:25:32.440 --> 00:25:35.640
But, I also got serious therapy during

00:25:34.240 --> 00:25:37.520
this time because the situation was

00:25:35.640 --> 00:25:39.720
genuinely so hard to live through. There

00:25:37.520 --> 00:25:42.080
were many days when I was in pain, my

00:25:39.720 --> 00:25:43.960
body felt terrible. 1 month of being on

00:25:42.080 --> 00:25:45.320
such antibiotics completely just [music]

00:25:43.960 --> 00:25:47.160
destroyed my health and I was just

00:25:45.320 --> 00:25:50.000
dealing with that physical recovery of

00:25:47.160 --> 00:25:51.520
it, the scarring, the anxiety, but I

00:25:50.000 --> 00:25:53.120
didn't want to feel bad about myself. I

00:25:51.520 --> 00:25:54.987
needed to get better, which is why I

00:25:53.120 --> 00:25:56.800
didn't stop my life just so I can,

00:25:54.987 --> 00:25:58.800
[music] you know, focus on my trauma.

00:25:56.800 --> 00:26:00.760
So, I focused instead on rebuilding my

00:25:58.800 --> 00:26:04.440
health from [music] every single angle I

00:26:00.760 --> 00:26:05.840
could, physical, mental, spiritual. So,

00:26:04.440 --> 00:26:07.400
how did I pick myself up at the same

00:26:05.840 --> 00:26:09.440
time? Like, I had to find a way to

00:26:07.400 --> 00:26:10.560
continue filming videos and this is

00:26:09.440 --> 00:26:12.440
something that most people never knew

00:26:10.560 --> 00:26:14.160
about. If I didn't want people to know

00:26:12.440 --> 00:26:15.920
what was going on and what I was going

00:26:14.160 --> 00:26:17.240
through, how am I supposed to hide this?

00:26:15.920 --> 00:26:18.720
The only way I could appear on camera

00:26:17.240 --> 00:26:21.760
during that time was by using special

00:26:18.720 --> 00:26:24.520
effects makeup. I literally sculpted a

00:26:21.760 --> 00:26:26.920
temporary prosthetic nose tip using nose

00:26:24.520 --> 00:26:29.240
wax, which is the same material used in

00:26:26.920 --> 00:26:31.680
Halloween and film makeup to create fake

00:26:29.240 --> 00:26:33.840
noses and facial prosthetics. I watched

00:26:31.680 --> 00:26:36.160
so many tutorial videos, I practiced it

00:26:33.840 --> 00:26:38.080
a bunch, and if I applied it correctly,

00:26:36.160 --> 00:26:40.640
it would smooth out the damaged area and

00:26:38.080 --> 00:26:42.880
make my nose look somewhat normal on

00:26:40.640 --> 00:26:44.800
camera. And honestly, it gave me a lot

00:26:42.880 --> 00:26:46.040
of hope. It may have even saved me. I

00:26:44.800 --> 00:26:48.160
also spoke with a lot of therapists

00:26:46.040 --> 00:26:49.560
during this time and they all agreed I

00:26:48.160 --> 00:26:52.040
will be able to recover from this

00:26:49.560 --> 00:26:54.040
mentally once the stressor is gone,

00:26:52.040 --> 00:26:56.280
meaning once I fix this. [music] So,

00:26:54.040 --> 00:26:58.520
while I was healing, I actually also got

00:26:56.280 --> 00:27:00.320
my chest implants, one of the smallest

00:26:58.520 --> 00:27:02.320
and safest kinds you can get. I barely

00:27:00.320 --> 00:27:04.040
even went up a size. But, I went to a

00:27:02.320 --> 00:27:05.920
surgeon here in Miami. She's incredible.

00:27:04.040 --> 00:27:07.720
She cares so much about patients, which

00:27:05.920 --> 00:27:09.280
gave me confidence like, "See, things

00:27:07.720 --> 00:27:11.040
can go well for me. Lightning will not

00:27:09.280 --> 00:27:13.160
strike twice for me." And, I was being

00:27:11.040 --> 00:27:15.040
very conservative with what I got, which

00:27:13.160 --> 00:27:17.200
is also very nice. Like, I love how it

00:27:15.040 --> 00:27:19.040
looks. Because before that, I had a

00:27:17.200 --> 00:27:20.138
deformities on my chest, too, and I

00:27:19.040 --> 00:27:20.200
wanted to fix

00:27:20.138 --> 00:27:21.960
>> [music]

00:27:20.200 --> 00:27:23.280
>> the deformities. Another thing that

00:27:21.960 --> 00:27:24.360
helped me mentally was knowing that my

00:27:23.280 --> 00:27:26.200
surgeon was willing to take

00:27:24.360 --> 00:27:28.080
responsibility for what happened and

00:27:26.200 --> 00:27:29.640
help fix things. But, before that could

00:27:28.080 --> 00:27:31.720
happen, we still had that one final step

00:27:29.640 --> 00:27:33.160
ahead, which was the revision surgery

00:27:31.720 --> 00:27:34.800
that would determine whether my nose

00:27:33.160 --> 00:27:36.000
would truly be rebuilt [music] after

00:27:34.800 --> 00:27:37.560
everything that the infection had

00:27:36.000 --> 00:27:39.040
destroyed. So, that was one of the

00:27:37.560 --> 00:27:40.760
hardest parts of my year was how my life

00:27:39.040 --> 00:27:41.920
didn't stop. I didn't let it stop. I was

00:27:40.760 --> 00:27:43.200
still running my business. I was still

00:27:41.920 --> 00:27:45.680
creating my content. I was still

00:27:43.200 --> 00:27:47.760
responsible for what I promised to other

00:27:45.680 --> 00:27:50.160
people, which included my first group

00:27:47.760 --> 00:27:52.000
trip that I hosted last summer in Crete

00:27:50.160 --> 00:27:53.680
in Greece. And, at that point, my nose

00:27:52.000 --> 00:27:56.320
still looked very damaged. So, every

00:27:53.680 --> 00:27:58.840
single day of that trip, I was wearing

00:27:56.320 --> 00:28:01.520
the prosthetic that I made with special

00:27:58.840 --> 00:28:04.360
effects nose wax. And, internally, I had

00:28:01.520 --> 00:28:05.880
so much anxiety. I kept wondering if

00:28:04.360 --> 00:28:07.640
people could sense that something was

00:28:05.880 --> 00:28:09.600
wrong with me. And, I even considered

00:28:07.640 --> 00:28:10.720
canceling the trip several times because

00:28:09.600 --> 00:28:12.720
I wasn't sure if I could show up for

00:28:10.720 --> 00:28:14.720
everyone. But, I know people have been

00:28:12.720 --> 00:28:16.800
looking forward to this experience for

00:28:14.720 --> 00:28:18.920
months. Many of them had planned their

00:28:16.800 --> 00:28:21.000
travel. They had to take time off around

00:28:18.920 --> 00:28:23.360
it. And, I didn't want to take that away

00:28:21.000 --> 00:28:25.040
from them. So, I decided to make it

00:28:23.360 --> 00:28:26.680
happen anyway. And, [music] I'm glad

00:28:25.040 --> 00:28:29.120
because the trip ended up being

00:28:26.680 --> 00:28:31.120
incredibly beautiful and healing for

00:28:29.120 --> 00:28:32.360
everyone involved, including myself.

00:28:31.120 --> 00:28:33.960
Many people told me it was one of the

00:28:32.360 --> 00:28:36.280
most transformative experiences they've

00:28:33.960 --> 00:28:37.440
ever had. And, I I think some people did

00:28:36.280 --> 00:28:39.280
figure out something was going on with

00:28:37.440 --> 00:28:40.480
my nose, but nobody said a word to me.

00:28:39.280 --> 00:28:41.920
But, if someone had asked me, I think I

00:28:40.480 --> 00:28:43.320
would have told them. For me, it was

00:28:41.920 --> 00:28:45.320
also healing in a different way. It

00:28:43.320 --> 00:28:47.120
reminded me that even during one of the

00:28:45.320 --> 00:28:48.880
hardest periods of my life, I was still

00:28:47.120 --> 00:28:50.520
capable of showing up anyway and

00:28:48.880 --> 00:28:52.440
creating something meaningful for other

00:28:50.520 --> 00:28:55.240
people. Even though there were many

00:28:52.440 --> 00:28:57.080
times during that trip itself when I

00:28:55.240 --> 00:28:59.800
would be in the bathroom like secretly

00:28:57.080 --> 00:29:01.720
crying because something had gone on

00:28:59.800 --> 00:29:04.280
with the nose prosthetic, something

00:29:01.720 --> 00:29:05.800
shifted, or my makeup looked weird, and

00:29:04.280 --> 00:29:07.480
I would cry. About a month after that

00:29:05.800 --> 00:29:09.120
group trip ended, it was finally time

00:29:07.480 --> 00:29:10.600
for me to deal with that last step in

00:29:09.120 --> 00:29:12.840
this whole situation, which was the

00:29:10.600 --> 00:29:15.360
revision surgery. So, about a month

00:29:12.840 --> 00:29:17.280
after my retreat ended, I flew back to

00:29:15.360 --> 00:29:19.560
Turkey [music] for the revision. So,

00:29:17.280 --> 00:29:22.200
yeah, I have to wake up at 5:00 a.m.

00:29:19.560 --> 00:29:23.880
tomorrow and be at the hospital at 6:00

00:29:22.200 --> 00:29:25.760
a.m. and I'll have my consultation with

00:29:23.880 --> 00:29:27.200
doctor tomorrow morning. I prefer

00:29:25.760 --> 00:29:29.360
surgery, so I don't know if I'm going to

00:29:27.200 --> 00:29:31.840
be the first [music] surgery of the day

00:29:29.360 --> 00:29:33.480
or second or whatever it is. I guess

00:29:31.840 --> 00:29:36.320
we'll find [music] out. But yeah, here's

00:29:33.480 --> 00:29:38.120
the last look at my nose. Mm.

00:29:36.320 --> 00:29:42.040
But yeah, I'm so tired of this. I'm so

00:29:38.120 --> 00:29:42.040
tired. So relieved, you guys.

00:29:42.320 --> 00:29:47.080
Oh, hey, MTV. I wasn't expecting you.

