00:39:01.520 --> 00:39:05.800
where medical costs are extremely high.

00:39:04.160 --> 00:39:07.680
So, thank God I had health insurance,

00:39:05.800 --> 00:39:09.440
but now I'm just so grateful [music]

00:39:07.680 --> 00:39:11.680
that the revision surgery was a success,

00:39:09.440 --> 00:39:13.240
my nose is normal, the infection was

00:39:11.680 --> 00:39:15.160
gone. Like being able to look normal

00:39:13.240 --> 00:39:17.120
again without relying on makeup or

00:39:15.160 --> 00:39:18.027
prosthetics had really helped my mental

00:39:17.120 --> 00:39:18.200
health so

00:39:18.027 --> 00:39:20.400
>> [music]

00:39:18.200 --> 00:39:23.000
>> tremendously. But do I regret getting

00:39:20.400 --> 00:39:24.720
the surgery? My answer is actually no.

00:39:23.000 --> 00:39:26.440
The complication itself was not because

00:39:24.720 --> 00:39:28.080
I was negligent. I did everything I

00:39:26.440 --> 00:39:30.000
could. But the real lesson here was

00:39:28.080 --> 00:39:32.280
learning how complex and unpredictable

00:39:30.000 --> 00:39:34.200
these surgeries can be and how important

00:39:32.280 --> 00:39:36.200
informed consent truly is. People

00:39:34.200 --> 00:39:37.800
discuss cosmetic surgery like it's so

00:39:36.200 --> 00:39:39.280
simple. You know, just have some money

00:39:37.800 --> 00:39:41.520
and some time and anybody can do it, but

00:39:39.280 --> 00:39:43.360
it's still irreversible, it has risks,

00:39:41.520 --> 00:39:44.920
it has recovery times people may not

00:39:43.360 --> 00:39:46.520
factor into, and there's potentially

00:39:44.920 --> 00:39:48.480
unexpected outcomes, potentially

00:39:46.520 --> 00:39:50.200
dangerous outcomes. When you pay for a

00:39:48.480 --> 00:39:51.560
cosmetic procedure, you're not just

00:39:50.200 --> 00:39:52.560
paying for the surgery itself. You have

00:39:51.560 --> 00:39:54.520
to pay for the whole process,

00:39:52.560 --> 00:39:56.040
post-surgical healing, follow-up care,

00:39:54.520 --> 00:39:57.400
and sometimes additional treatments. And

00:39:56.040 --> 00:39:59.560
now I'm going to wear like

00:39:57.400 --> 00:40:00.760
I don't know. If there's an emergency

00:39:59.560 --> 00:40:02.960
like what happened to me, these

00:40:00.760 --> 00:40:04.280
realities are just rarely talked about.

00:40:02.960 --> 00:40:05.640
And I see people just like casually

00:40:04.280 --> 00:40:06.880
recommend like surgery to other people

00:40:05.640 --> 00:40:08.440
without fully understanding what the

00:40:06.880 --> 00:40:09.720
hell they're talking about. I recently

00:40:08.440 --> 00:40:11.080
spoke to someone who's bald and he told

00:40:09.720 --> 00:40:12.800
me that people constantly tell him like

00:40:11.080 --> 00:40:13.960
just get a hair transplant. Nobody

00:40:12.800 --> 00:40:15.520
should be recommending something like

00:40:13.960 --> 00:40:17.240
that in such a cavalier and

00:40:15.520 --> 00:40:18.920
irresponsible way. Anyone who has

00:40:17.240 --> 00:40:21.120
experienced surgical complications or is

00:40:18.920 --> 00:40:22.840
a doctor will understand how serious

00:40:21.120 --> 00:40:26.280
these decisions can be. It's like how

00:40:22.840 --> 00:40:28.600
you see LASIK doctors who wear glasses.

00:40:26.280 --> 00:40:30.680
Why are they wearing glasses if LASIK

00:40:28.600 --> 00:40:31.840
procedures are so effective? This is

00:40:30.680 --> 00:40:34.120
also why I don't tell people who my

00:40:31.840 --> 00:40:35.560
surgeon is when they ask me because now

00:40:34.120 --> 00:40:37.840
you know why and I know a lot of girlies

00:40:35.560 --> 00:40:39.440
they ask me. I'm not gatekeeping guys

00:40:37.840 --> 00:40:40.880
like I really cannot tell you because of

00:40:39.440 --> 00:40:41.840
what happened and now you know. So if

00:40:40.880 --> 00:40:43.240
anyone watching this video is

00:40:41.840 --> 00:40:45.640
considering rhinoplasty or any other

00:40:43.240 --> 00:40:48.080
cosmetic surgery my biggest advice is

00:40:45.640 --> 00:40:49.600
research deeply, speak with multiple

00:40:48.080 --> 00:40:51.040
surgeons, talk to real patients who have

00:40:49.600 --> 00:40:52.800
gone through the procedure, understand

00:40:51.040 --> 00:40:54.560
all the risk, the recovery process

00:40:52.800 --> 00:40:56.680
before making this decision. Make sure

00:40:54.560 --> 00:40:59.280
you have double the amount of money that

00:40:56.680 --> 00:41:01.480
the surgery cost so that you can cover

00:40:59.280 --> 00:41:02.840
any kind of post-surgical recovery.

00:41:01.480 --> 00:41:04.200
Because when you make that choice you're

00:41:02.840 --> 00:41:05.760
not just choosing a new look, you're

00:41:04.200 --> 00:41:06.920
signing up for a medical procedure that

00:41:05.760 --> 00:41:08.640
can change your life for better or

00:41:06.920 --> 00:41:10.360
worse. And I promise you that it's not

00:41:08.640 --> 00:41:11.760
